From b0230dad4d07d38015c2da9017a169a26049e7ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: krimvp <anton.balboa@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:56:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix: refuse a secret or model key shorter than 8 characters

The scrub replaces each raw secret value wherever it occurs in the run log,
JSON keys included. A 1-character WEATHER_API_KEY rewrote keys such as
"scenario" into "s[LEAKED:WEATHER_API_KEY]enario", the result directory no
longer parsed, and `aigent run` exited 4 after spending model calls.
runScenario now reports such a value as a scenario problem, so the CLI
exits 2 before the first session opens.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NrPUJ99oxaEND1KwMyA3iB
